cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured number, cite the artifact that produced it -- the numbers have intervals, and the intervals are the point."
title: "greenwash"
abstract: "A trust report on what a coding agent's \"done\" claim is actually worth. It reads a diff with static rules and runs the project's own tests -- including a baseline differential, a changed test's committed form, and an optional held-out suite -- then prints a verdict, a confidence, and the evidence behind both. Local, deterministic, dependency-free, no model and no network."
authors:
  - name: "greenwash contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0DukePan/greenwash"
url: "https://github.com/0DukePan/greenwash"
license: MIT
version: "0.4.2"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - coding-agents
  - reward-hacking
  - verification
  - software-testing
  - static-analysis
  - agent-evaluation
